{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SYugWwe8dWdGrXGYmNxeHf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# R70 — Tests/Docs review — Phase 9 metrics + evaluation\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** 9\n4\t**Type:** review\n5\t**Model class:** advanced\n6\t**Depends on:** T65, T66, T67, T68, T69\n7\t**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-9-metrics-and-evaluation)\n8\t**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`); Definition of Done checklist (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`).\n9\t\n10\t## Goal\n11\t\n12\tThis task delivers the Phase 9 review. It asserts that the metrics collection module (T65), the cross-language benchmark fixture repository (T66), the MCP-wired metrics surface (T67), the regression dashboard + CLI report (T68), and the regression coverage tests (T69) together satisfy spec §Phase 9 deliverables and definition of done, and that each spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target is either met by T69's tests or recorded as a `fail` finding triggering reopen. Without this review, Phase 10 (Human Review UI) proceeds against an unvalidated metrics layer and the success-criterion claims cannot be defended.\n13\t\n14\t## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n15\t\n16\t> \"Phase 9 Deliverables: retrieval relevance metrics; memory usefulness metrics; context token efficiency metrics; stale/contradicted memory surfacing metrics; test-pass-after-plan metrics; repeated-failure reduction metrics; benchmark tasks with golden expected anchors; regression dashboard or CLI report.\"\n17\t\n18\t> \"Required metrics: tool calls per successful task; irrelevant files opened per task; relevant anchor recall; memory inclusion precision; memory later-used rate; stale memory surfaced rate; contradiction missed rate; tests recommended versus tests needed; workflow success after first plan.\" (spec §Phase 9)\n19\t\n20\t> \"Initial targets: 30 percent fewer discovery tool calls on benchmark tasks; 40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads; 80 percent memory inclusion precision on curated memory benchmarks; zero trusted display of known contradicted memory; zero trusted display of known stale memory without stale label; 90 percent correct relevant-test recommendation on curated tasks.\" (spec §Measurable Success Criteria)\n21\t\n22\t> \"Definition of done: changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote.\" (spec §Phase 9)\n23\t\n24\t## Inputs\n25\t\n26\t- Dependency outputs:\n27\t  - T65 — `metrics/{mod, signals, signals_tests}.rs`.\n28\t  - T66 — `benches/fixtures/{README, rust-repo/manifest, typescript-repo/manifest, python-repo/manifest, golden_anchors.json}` + `cognitive_workspace_benchmark.rs`.\n29\t  - T67 — `rpc/{metrics_surface, metrics_surface_tests}.rs`.\n30\t  - T68 — `bin/lattice_report.rs`, `metrics/{report, report_tests}.rs`, `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md`.\n31\t  - T69 — `metrics/regression_tests.rs`.\n32\t- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n33\t  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json` (from T04) — baseline column referenced by T69.\n34\t  - The reviews directory `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/`.\n35\t- Standards: Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, `## Single source of truth`, `## No broken windows`, `## Schema / model parity`, `## Tests as documentation`, `## Observability`; Definition of Done checklist.\n36\t\n37\t## Steps\n38\t\n39\t1. Read spec §Phase 9 and §Measurable Success Criteria in full. Quote the \"Required metrics\" paragraph and the \"Initial targets\" paragraph verbatim at the top of the review.\n40\t2. Under `## Spec alignment`, walk every Phase 9 deliverable (retrieval relevance metrics, memory usefulness metrics, context token efficiency metrics, stale/contradicted memory surfacing metrics, test-pass-after-plan metrics, repeated-failure reduction metrics, benchmark tasks with golden expected anchors, regression dashboard/CLI report) and cite the implementing files from T65–T69. Flag any deliverable that is missing or partial.\n41\t3. Under `## Coding-standard alignment`, run a per-file check across `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs`, and `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/cognitive_workspace_benchmark.rs`: file length ≤800 lines, function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10, schema parity (every public type serde-derived), no `TODO`/`FIXME`/commented-out code, no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`, observability spans present, honest `None` reporting on missing data (no fabricated zeros). Record each violation with file:line.\n42\t4. Under `## Success-criteria coverage`, build a matrix of every spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target (six rows: 30% discovery, 40% irrelevant reads, 80% memory precision, 0 stale-without-label, 0 contradicted-trusted, 90% test recommendation). For each row, cite the T69 `#[test]` name proving the target, the current measured value on the T66 fixtures, the baseline value from T04, and the pass/fail outcome. Any row without a passing test is a `fail` finding.\n43\t5. Under `## Findings`, summarize spec gaps, coding-standard violations, threshold-coverage misses, fixture coverage gaps (e.g. one language fixture missing a task class), honest-null violations, and any divergence between the T68 CLI report output and the T65 collector. Each finding cites file:line and the spec or standard it violates.\n44\t6. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib metrics` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::metrics_surface_tests` and `cd daemon && cargo bench --bench cognitive_workspace_benchmark -- --warm-up-time 1 --measurement-time 3`. Record each result in the review.\n45\t7. Under `## Verdict`, state `pass` or `fail` with a one-paragraph justification. If `fail`, name the specific tasks that must be reopened.\n46\t8. Save the review at `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` with the mandatory headings checked by verification commands.\n47\t\n48\t## Files expected\n49\t\n50\t- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — structured Phase 9 review with `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Success-criteria coverage`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict` headings; per-deliverable spec citations; per-file standard checks; per-target threshold matrix; build/test/bench results; verdict with reopen list if `fail`.\n51\t\n52\t## Verification\n53\t\n54\t- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — confirms the review exists at the harness path.\n55\t- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — confirms spec alignment is recorded under a dedicated heading.\n56\t- `grep -q '## Success-criteria coverage' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — confirms the threshold matrix is recorded under a dedicated heading rather than buried in prose.\n57\t- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — confirms a verdict is stated under a dedicated heading.\n58\t\n59\t## Coding-standard checks\n60\t\n61\t- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md`).\n62\t- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — not applicable (review doc).\n63\t- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n64\t- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.\n65\t- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming — not applicable (review doc).\n66\t- For schema changes: review must flag any divergence between T67's MCP surface, T68's CLI report, and T65's canonical types as a contract gate failure.\n67\t- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation`, `## Measurable Success Criteria`, `## Risks` (specifically \"Overfitting To Current Repo\"); reference `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` from T68 and `benches/fixtures/README.md` from T66.\n68\t\n69\t## Definition of done\n70\t\n71\t- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n72\t- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n73\t- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n74\t- [ ] No deferred work: every Phase 9 spec deliverable and every spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target is either covered with a passing test or recorded as a `fail` finding triggering reopen of the corresponding T-task.\n75\t- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dcdb14de-3541-4532-8220-c4c3ddb6207e","uuid":"3f2acca2-7aef-48ca-b06d-7c2ae6eebbd7","timestamp":"2026-05-17T16:38:18.771Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R70.md","content":"# R70 — Tests/Docs review — Phase 9 metrics + evaluation\n\n**Phase:** 9\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T65, T66, T67, T68, T69\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-9-metrics-and-evaluation)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`); Definition of Done checklist (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers the Phase 9 review. It asserts that the metrics collection module (T65), the cross-language benchmark fixture repository (T66), the MCP-wired metrics surface (T67), the regression dashboard + CLI report (T68), and the regression coverage tests (T69) together satisfy spec §Phase 9 deliverables and definition of done, and that each spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target is either met by T69's tests or recorded as a `fail` finding triggering reopen. Without this review, Phase 10 (Human Review UI) proceeds against an unvalidated metrics layer and the success-criterion claims cannot be defended.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 9 Deliverables: retrieval relevance metrics; memory usefulness metrics; context token efficiency metrics; stale/contradicted memory surfacing metrics; test-pass-after-plan metrics; repeated-failure reduction metrics; benchmark tasks with golden expected anchors; regression dashboard or CLI report.\"\n\n> \"Required metrics: tool calls per successful task; irrelevant files opened per task; relevant anchor recall; memory inclusion precision; memory later-used rate; stale memory surfaced rate; contradiction missed rate; tests recommended versus tests needed; workflow success after first plan.\" (spec §Phase 9)\n\n> \"Initial targets: 30 percent fewer discovery tool calls on benchmark tasks; 40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads; 80 percent memory inclusion precision on curated memory benchmarks; zero trusted display of known contradicted memory; zero trusted display of known stale memory without stale label; 90 percent correct relevant-test recommendation on curated tasks.\" (spec §Measurable Success Criteria)\n\n> \"Definition of done: changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote.\" (spec §Phase 9)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T65 — `metrics/{mod, signals, signals_tests}.rs`.\n  - T66 — `benches/fixtures/{README, rust-repo/manifest, typescript-repo/manifest, python-repo/manifest, golden_anchors.json}` + `cognitive_workspace_benchmark.rs`.\n  - T67 — `rpc/{metrics_surface, metrics_surface_tests}.rs`.\n  - T68 — `bin/lattice_report.rs`, `metrics/{report, report_tests}.rs`, `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md`.\n  - T69 — `metrics/regression_tests.rs`.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json` (from T04) — baseline column referenced by T69.\n  - The reviews directory `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/`.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, `## Single source of truth`, `## No broken windows`, `## Schema / model parity`, `## Tests as documentation`, `## Observability`; Definition of Done checklist.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 9 and §Measurable Success Criteria in full. Quote the \"Required metrics\" paragraph and the \"Initial targets\" paragraph verbatim at the top of the review.\n2. Under `## Spec alignment`, walk every Phase 9 deliverable (retrieval relevance metrics, memory usefulness metrics, context token efficiency metrics, stale/contradicted memory surfacing metrics, test-pass-after-plan metrics, repeated-failure reduction metrics, benchmark tasks with golden expected anchors, regression dashboard/CLI report) and cite the implementing files from T65–T69. Flag any deliverable that is missing or partial.\n3. Under `## Coding-standard alignment`, run a per-file check across `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs`, and `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/cognitive_workspace_benchmark.rs`: file length ≤800 lines, function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10, schema parity (every public type serde-derived), no `TODO`/`FIXME`/commented-out code, no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`, observability spans present, honest `None` reporting on missing data (no fabricated zeros). Record each violation with file:line.\n4. Under `## Success-criteria coverage`, build a matrix of every spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target (six rows: 30% discovery, 40% irrelevant reads, 80% memory precision, 0 stale-without-label, 0 contradicted-trusted, 90% test recommendation). For each row, cite the T69 `#[test]` name proving the target, the current measured value on the T66 fixtures, the baseline value from T04, and the pass/fail outcome. Any row without a passing test is a `fail` finding.\n5. Under `## Findings`, summarize spec gaps, coding-standard violations, threshold-coverage misses, fixture coverage gaps (e.g. one language fixture missing a task class), honest-null violations, and any divergence between the T68 CLI report output and the T65 collector. Each finding cites file:line and the spec or standard it violates.\n6. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib metrics` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::metrics_surface_tests` and `cd daemon && cargo bench --bench cognitive_workspace_benchmark -- --warm-up-time 1 --measurement-time 3`. Record each result in the review.\n7. Under `## Verdict`, state `pass` or `fail` with a one-paragraph justification. If `fail`, name the specific tasks that must be reopened.\n8. Save the review at `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` with the mandatory headings checked by verification commands.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — structured Phase 9 review with `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Success-criteria coverage`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict` headings; per-deliverable spec citations; per-file standard checks; per-target threshold matrix; build/test/bench results; verdict with reopen list if `fail`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — confirms the review exists at the harness path.\n- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — confirms spec alignment is recorded under a dedicated heading.\n- `grep -q '## Success-criteria coverage' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — confirms the threshold matrix is recorded under a dedicated heading rather than buried in prose.\n- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md` — confirms a verdict is stated under a dedicated heading.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R70-metrics.md`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — not applicable (review doc).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming — not applicable (review doc).\n- For schema changes: review must flag any divergence between T67's MCP surface, T68's CLI report, and T65's canonical types as a contract gate failure.\n- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation`, `## Measurable Success Criteria`, `## Risks` (specifically \"Overfitting To Current Repo\"); reference `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` from T68 and `benches/fixtures/README.md` from T66.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every Phase 9 spec deliverable and every spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target is either covered with a passing test or recorded as a `fail` finding triggering reopen of the corresponding T-task.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed.\n","numLines":76,"startLine":1,"totalLines":76}}}
